-        "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice. Let $\\omega_t$ be a smooth finite signed vorticity density on $[0,T]\\times\\mathbb R^2$ with finite first moment, transported by a sign-preserving characteristic flow $X_t$ satisfying $\\omega_t=(X_t)_\\#\\omega_0$ and $\\dot X_t(x)=(K*\\omega_t)(X_t(x))$, where $K$ is the singular kernel in [[def-mollified-biot-savart-vortex-kernel]]. Assume $\\sup_{t\\le T}\\|\\omega_t\\|_\\infty\\le W$, $\\int\\sup_{t\\le T}|X_t(x)|d|\\omega_0|(x)<\\infty$, and the flow transports each Jordan part to the corresponding Jordan part. Put $M=|\\omega_0|(\\mathbb R^2)$. Let $$\\omega_N^0=\\sum_{i=1}^N\\Gamma_i\\delta_{x_i^0}$$ be a finite signed particle measure whose positive and negative Jordan masses respectively equal those of $\\omega_0$, with finite first moment, and with consolidated atoms whose positive and negative supports are disjoint; thus $\\sum_i|\\Gamma_i|=M$. Let $E_0=C_{\\pm}(\\omega_0,\\omega_N^0)<\\infty$.  Fix $\\varepsilon>0$. For every time and force location $(t,x)$, suppose the force integrand $F_{t,x}:R\\to\\mathbb R^2$ lies in $C^4(R,\\mathbb R^2)$ and its fourth partial derivatives satisfy the uniform bounds $M_{40},M_{04}$. Let the tensor Simpson evaluator use the even panel counts and widths in [[thm-tensor-simpson-force-error]], and define its residual by $r_q(t,x)=Q_yQ_xF_{t,x}-\\int_R F_{t,x}$. Thus $$\\eta_q=\\frac{\\sqrt2|R|}{180}(h_x^4M_{40}+h_y^4M_{04}).$$ Assume this residual is the same correction function for every particle, $\\sup_{t,x}|r_q(t,x)|\\le\\eta_q$, and the corrected regularized particle flow preserves the two Jordan parts. Write $x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}$ for the exact solution from $x_i^0$ of $$\\dot x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)=\\sum_{j=1}^N\\Gamma_jK_\\varepsilon(x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)-x_j^{\\varepsilon,q}(t))+r_q(t,x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)),$$ and set $\\omega_N^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)=\\sum_i\\Gamma_i\\delta_{x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)}$. Assume $r_q$ and the resulting finite-dimensional particle field are jointly $C^4$ in time and state with derivatives through order four bounded on a compact tube containing all exact paths and RK4 stages. Let $x_i^h(T)$ be the RK4 states from the same initial data for this ODE, and define $\\omega_{N,h}^{\\varepsilon,q}(T)=\\sum_i\\Gamma_i\\delta_{x_i^h(T)}$. Let $h=T/n\\le h_0$ for an integer $n\\ge1$ and define $C_{RK}:=C_4(e^{L_*T}-1)/L_*$ if $L_*>0$, and $C_{RK}:=C_4T$ if $L_*=0$, where $C_4,L_*,h_0$ are the constants in [[thm-rk4-global-error-for-regularized-vortex-particles]]. Then $$d_{BL}(\\omega_T,\\omega_{N,h}^{\\varepsilon,q}(T)) \\le e^{2L_\\varepsilon MT}\\left(E_0+MT\\left(C_\\rho\\varepsilon W+\\eta_q\\right)\\right)+MC_{RK}h^4,$$ where $L_\\varepsilon$ is a one-variable global Lipschitz constant for $K_\\varepsilon$; the induced two-variable constant for $K_\\varepsilon(x-y)$ is also $L_\\varepsilon$. The terms are initial signed particle approximation, blob regularization, force quadrature, and RK4 time error. The constants may depend on $\\varepsilon$, particle count, and the tube; no uniform singular limit as $\\varepsilon\\to0$ is claimed.",
+        "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice. Let $\\omega_t$ be a smooth finite signed vorticity density on $[0,T]\\times\\mathbb R^2$ with finite first moment, transported by a sign-preserving characteristic flow $X_t$ satisfying $\\omega_t=(X_t)_\\#\\omega_0$ and $\\dot X_t(x)=(K*\\omega_t)(X_t(x))$, where $K$ is the singular kernel in [[def-mollified-biot-savart-vortex-kernel]]. Assume $\\sup_{t\\le T}\\|\\omega_t\\|_\\infty\\le W$, $\\int\\sup_{t\\le T}|X_t(x)|d|\\omega_0|(x)<\\infty$, and the flow transports each Jordan part to the corresponding Jordan part. Put $M=|\\omega_0|(\\mathbb R^2)$. Let\n$$\\omega_N^0=\\sum_{i=1}^N\\Gamma_i\\delta_{x_i^0}$$\nbe a finite signed particle measure whose positive and negative Jordan masses respectively equal those of $\\omega_0$, with finite first moment, and with consolidated atoms whose positive and negative supports are disjoint; thus $\\sum_i|\\Gamma_i|=M$. Let $E_0=C_{\\pm}(\\omega_0,\\omega_N^0)<\\infty$.\n\nFix $\\varepsilon>0$. For every time and force location $(t,x)$, suppose the force integrand $F_{t,x}:R\\to\\mathbb R^2$ lies in $C^4(R,\\mathbb R^2)$ and its fourth partial derivatives satisfy the uniform bounds $M_{40},M_{04}$. Let the tensor Simpson evaluator use the even panel counts and widths in [[thm-tensor-simpson-force-error]], and define its residual by $r_q(t,x)=Q_yQ_xF_{t,x}-\\int_R F_{t,x}$. Thus\n$$\\eta_q=\\frac{\\sqrt2|R|}{180}(h_x^4M_{40}+h_y^4M_{04}).$$\nAssume this residual is the same correction function for every particle, $\\sup_{t,x}|r_q(t,x)|\\le\\eta_q$, and the corrected regularized particle flow preserves the two Jordan parts. Write $x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}$ for the exact solution from $x_i^0$ of\n$$\\dot x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)=\\sum_{j=1}^N\\Gamma_jK_\\varepsilon(x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)-x_j^{\\varepsilon,q}(t))+r_q(t,x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)),$$\nand set $\\omega_N^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)=\\sum_i\\Gamma_i\\delta_{x_i^{\\varepsilon,q}(t)}$. Assume $r_q$ and the resulting finite-dimensional particle field are jointly $C^4$ in time and state with derivatives through order four bounded on a compact tube containing all exact paths and RK4 stages. Let $x_i^h(T)$ be the RK4 states from the same initial data for this ODE, and define $\\omega_{N,h}^{\\varepsilon,q}(T)=\\sum_i\\Gamma_i\\delta_{x_i^h(T)}$. Let $h=T/n\\le h_0$ for an integer $n\\ge1$ and define $C_{RK}:=C_4(e^{L_*T}-1)/L_*$ if $L_*>0$, and $C_{RK}:=C_4T$ if $L_*=0$, where $C_4,L_*,h_0$ are the constants in [[thm-rk4-global-error-for-regularized-vortex-particles]]. Then\n$$d_{BL}(\\omega_T,\\omega_{N,h}^{\\varepsilon,q}(T)) \\le e^{2L_\\varepsilon MT}\\left(E_0+MT\\left(C_\\rho\\varepsilon W+\\eta_q\\right)\\right)+MC_{RK}h^4,$$\nwhere $L_\\varepsilon$ is a one-variable global Lipschitz constant for $K_\\varepsilon$; the induced two-variable constant for $K_\\varepsilon(x-y)$ is also $L_\\varepsilon$. The terms are initial signed particle approximation, blob regularization, force quadrature, and RK4 time error. The constants may depend on $\\varepsilon$, particle count, and the tube; no uniform singular limit as $\\varepsilon\\to0$ is claimed.\n\nThe RK4 tube condition in the Statement includes all numerical grid states and every stage generated at each grid step from both the exact solution start and the numerical start; both one-step maps are defined.",
