-          "quote": "Input a rectangle $R=[a,b]\\times[c,d]$ with $a<b$, $c<d$, even integers $n_x,n_y\\ge2$, and an exact evaluation oracle for $F:R\\to\\mathbb R^2$. Return status invalid-domain if either interval is degenerate or reversed, and status invalid-panel-count if either panel count is not an even integer at least two. Otherwise set $h_x=(b-a)/n_x$, $h_y=(d-c)/n_y$, apply [[alg-composite-simpson-rule]] componentwise in the $x$ direction and then the $y$ direction, and return the resulting tensor sum $Q_yQ_xF$. If an evaluation oracle reports an unavailable value, stop at the first such grid point and return evaluation-failure with that point. The exact-real procedure makes finitely many evaluations and sums. This definition makes no floating-point roundoff or force-accuracy claim; error control is a separate result.\n",
+          "quote": "Input real endpoints $a,b,c,d$, integer panel counts $n_x,n_y$, and an exact evaluation oracle that, when queried at a point, returns either a value in $\\mathbb R^2$ or evaluation-failure. First, if $a\\ge b$ or $c\\ge d$, return invalid-domain without querying the oracle. Next, if either panel count is odd or is less than two, return invalid-panel-count without querying the oracle. For the remaining inputs set $R=[a,b]\\times[c,d]$, $h_x=(b-a)/n_x$, $h_y=(d-c)/n_y$, $x_i=a+ih_x$ for $0\\le i\\le n_x$, and $y_j=c+jh_y$ for $0\\le j\\le n_y$. Query the oracle at every grid point in lexicographic order with $i$ first and $j$ second, storing the returned values. If a query fails, stop at the first such point and return evaluation-failure with that point. Otherwise, for each $j$ form the continuous piecewise-linear interpolant through the stored values $F(x_i,y_j)$ and apply [[alg-composite-simpson-rule]] componentwise in $x$ to this interpolant, obtaining $G_j=Q_xF(\\cdot,y_j)$. Form the continuous piecewise-linear interpolant through the stored $G_j$ and apply the same valid Simpson procedure componentwise in $y$ to obtain $Q_yG=Q_yQ_xF$. Each interpolant is queried only at its stored grid nodes, so no new oracle call is needed. Both calls to the supplier use strictly ordered endpoints and even panel counts at least two. This exact-real procedure makes finitely many evaluations and sums; it makes no floating-point roundoff or force-accuracy claim, and error control is a separate result.",
