-          "quote": "Assume AC and Countable Choice. Let $K_\\varepsilon$ have one-variable Lipschitz constant $L_\\varepsilon$; then $(x,y)\\mapsto K_\\varepsilon(x-y)$ has two-variable constant $L_\\varepsilon$. Let $\\omega_0,\\nu_0$ have separately matching positive and negative Jordan masses and total variation mass $M$. For $M>0$, use the Jordan-label probability spaces of [[def-signed-vorticity-characteristic-solution]] and suppose their path maps $X^\\omega_t(x,s)$ and $X^\\nu_t(y,s)$ have integrable time suprema, satisfy $X^\\omega_0(x,s)=x$ and $X^\\nu_0(y,s)=y$, and represent $\\omega_t,\\nu_t$ by the signed pushforward formula there. Assume at each time the positive and negative label pushforwards are the Jordan parts. Write\n$$u^\\omega_t(x)=\\int K_\\varepsilon(x-z)d\\omega_t(z),\\qquad u^\\nu_t(y)=\\int K_\\varepsilon(y-z)d\\nu_t(z).$$\nSuppose their absolutely continuous sign-labelled trajectories satisfy\n$$\\dot X^\\omega_t(x,s)=u^\\omega_t(X^\\omega_t(x,s))+r_\\omega(t,x,s),\\qquad \\dot X^\\nu_t(y,s)=u^\\nu_t(X^\\nu_t(y,s))+r_\\nu(t,y,s)$$\nfor almost every time and almost every label of sign $s\\in\\{+,-\\}$, with $|r_\\omega|\\le\\eta_\\omega$ and $|r_\\nu|\\le\\eta_\\nu$ on $[0,T]$. For every prescribed initial pair of sign-preserving couplings of total cost $D_0$,\n$$d_{BL}(\\omega_t,\\nu_t)\\le C_{\\pm}(\\omega_t,\\nu_t)\\le e^{2L_\\varepsilon Mt}\\bigl(D_0+M(\\eta_\\omega+\\eta_\\nu)t\\bigr).$$\nIf $M=0$, both curves are zero and the inequalities hold with zero right side. Taking the infimum over initial couplings in the $M>0$ case gives the same bound with $D_0=C_{\\pm}(\\omega_0,\\nu_0)$, without assuming attainment.\n\n",
